1
00:00:03,095 --> 00:00:05,017
Way up high, above the Earth,

2
00:00:05,067 --> 00:00:07,737
Noah and Mila are floating inside Curio!

3
00:00:07,787 --> 00:00:08,332
But why?

4
00:00:09,145 --> 00:00:11,208
When Mila lets go of her pencil,

5
00:00:11,258 --> 00:00:12,265
it doesn't fall!

6
00:00:12,315 --> 00:00:15,088
So, in space, is there no gravity anymore?

7
00:00:15,872 --> 00:00:17,386
Discovery mission!

8
00:00:19,915 --> 00:00:20,612
Mini mode!

9
00:00:20,662 --> 00:00:23,075
We drop a box with a ball inside.

10
00:00:23,125 --> 00:00:24,120
The box falls…

11
00:00:24,170 --> 00:00:26,135
and the ball falls with it,

12
00:00:26,185 --> 00:00:27,479
at the same speed.

13
00:00:27,529 --> 00:00:29,768
So, inside the box, it floats!

14
00:00:30,609 --> 00:00:33,353
Throw a ball, and it falls to the ground.

15
00:00:33,403 --> 00:00:34,988
Harder, it goes further.

16
00:00:35,038 --> 00:00:36,010
And super hard?

17
00:00:36,060 --> 00:00:37,033
It still falls…

18
00:00:37,083 --> 00:00:40,081
but it misses the Earth, and goes around it!

19
00:00:40,871 --> 00:00:41,765
That's an orbit!

20
00:00:41,815 --> 00:00:45,130
Curio goes so fast that it falls while missing the Earth,

21
00:00:45,180 --> 00:00:45,956
over and over.

22
00:00:46,006 --> 00:00:48,140
And since Noah and Mila fall with it…

23
00:00:48,190 --> 00:00:48,840
they float!

24
00:00:49,871 --> 00:00:51,718
Real astronauts are the same:

25
00:00:51,768 --> 00:00:54,138
their station falls around the Earth.

26
00:00:54,188 --> 00:00:54,989
And up there,

27
00:00:55,039 --> 00:00:57,393
gravity is almost as strong as here!

28
00:00:58,170 --> 00:01:00,512
And that's why astronauts float.

29
00:01:01,671 --> 00:01:04,497
Astronauts float because they fall around the Earth,

30
00:01:04,547 --> 00:01:05,929
without ever reaching it.

31
00:01:06,711 --> 00:01:09,027
With an adult: jump off a small step.

32
00:01:09,077 --> 00:01:12,289
During the fall, your body doesn't feel its weight…

33
00:01:12,339 --> 00:01:14,066
one second as an astronaut!

34
00:01:14,851 --> 00:01:17,086
And why does the Moon change shape?

35
00:01:17,136 --> 00:01:18,442
The answer tomorrow.
